How about you smash gems (with a pick-axe? by throwing them?
with some special "alchemy kit" tool?), and turn them into powder.
Drop the powder into a potion of water, and you get a potion of 
(something else).  If you used worthless glass, it wouldn't work.

eg: dilithium crystal -> glowing potion
    diamond           -> smoky potion
    ruby              -> ruby potion
    sapphire          -> brilliant blue potion         
    emerald           -> emerald potion
    turquoise         -> cyan potion (not a perfect color match)
    aquamarine        -> fizzy potion (not a perfect color match)
    amber             -> orange potion
    topaz             -> yellow potion
    opal              -> cloudy potion
    garnet            -> pink potion            
    amethyst          -> purple-red potion
    jasper            -> puce potion
    fluorite          -> magenta potion     
    jade              -> dark green potion         

There are more potions than gems, so we would have to be slightly 
creative to get the following:
 -> sky blue potion
 -> milky potion (white)
 -> swirly potion (brown)
 -> bubbly potion (white)
 -> brown potion
 -> dark potion (black)
